1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for a certain day
drifting on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a whetstone,
even my shoes go flying,

3
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:32,860
onto the head of a carpenter
who was in a chokehold,

4
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I'm still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:44,200
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:49,280
a yawn or two, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels oddly gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed-hat water bottle,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls toward
the great observatory.

10
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:15,920
Why does tomorrow end too

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,740
Katsushika Shibamata, happy again, they say.

12
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:24,700
Running around everywhere,
I realized I'm such a fool.

13
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,440
I'd totally forgotten about it!

14
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:22,540
Yes! Super lucky!

15
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,540
This is truly a blessing from God!

16
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,147
Wait,

17
00:02:28,197 --> 00:02:32,140
I think the redemption period
for the Atari Baken is 60 days.

18
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:36,800
49, 50, 51, 52, 53, 54,

19
00:02:36,850 --> 00:02:40,340
55, 56, 57, 58, 59, 60?

20
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:44,620
If I don't exchange it today,
it'll become worthless!

21
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:52,120
I think the payout was about 1,000 yen, so

22
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:54,740
I nearly lost out on Zurumagen!

23
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,400
What should I spend it on?

24
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:04,120
Lucky again!

25
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:07,340
My winning ticket!

26
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:22,340
Thank goodness, you've finally come to.

27
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:24,440
Maria, where are we?

28
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:27,360
You could have stayed asleep a little longer,
you know.

29
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:32,500
Isn't that the old man from Hondara Gen?
What the hell is going on?

30
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:35,160
You're going to Canada.

31
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:36,000
What?

32
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:41,200
The truth is, our Hondara Kenpō has
decided to open a branch in Canada.

33
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,280
We're just about to leave
on a honeymoon with Ai.

34
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:46,280
And why do I have to come along?

35
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,520
I'll only go if it's with Ryo-san!

36
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:51,820
Ai said that,
so I had no choice but to bring you along.

37
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,820
Could it be that...

38
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:57,740
Was it you who hit me while
flashing that bundle of bills?

39
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:00,420
Listen!

40
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:03,480
I have to buy this betting ticket today!

41
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:04,360
Impossible!

42
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:06,280
Shut up!
Could you make it a hundred thousand yen?

43
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:08,400
Sir! Please stop!

44
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:11,680
Let go!
I have to go home and buy my betting ticket!

45
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:12,420
Ugh!

46
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:12,800
What!

47
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,200
Sir!

48
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:29,840
That's why I said it was impossible.

49
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:33,040
You dragged me all the way out
here while I was knocked out!

50
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:35,380
What are you going to
do about my 100,000 yen?

51
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:36,720
Don't get so worked up.

52
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:39,520
Once we get to Canada,
it'll be nothing but nice things!

53
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,620
Nice things?

54
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,560
In the village where we bought
land for the branch office,

55
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:46,320
apparently there are
loads of blonde bombshells.

56
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:50,149
Not Ai's padded, fake dad. I mean her real father,
her biological father.

57
00:04:50,199 --> 00:04:52,980
And F and G cups are the norm!

58
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,360
Her biological father?

59
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:07,882
No,

60
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:11,642
I've always wanted to
visit Canada at least once.

61
00:05:11,692 --> 00:05:13,500
Fine, I'll tag along with you.

62
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:17,000
I see. Alright,
let's go have some fun together.

63
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:19,340
You're well prepared, aren't you?

64
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:26,780
How delightful, how delightful!

65
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:29,580
So you're working away from your family?
That must be tough.

66
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:31,800
Over here we've got fresh milk, fresh milk!

67
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:35,320
Excuse me, sir,
that's your own responsibility.

68
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,960
Miss, you came at just the right time.

69
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:40,320
Please cheer this man up,
he's a pitiful guy.

70
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:44,040
Ryo-sama suddenly got in a good mood.
I wonder what happened to him.

71
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,750
Who knows. Anyway, Ai,

72
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:48,200
there's something I want to tell you.

73
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:54,220
Actually, I'm thinking of building a suite
for you two on the branch's planned site.

74
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:55,560
"You two"?

75
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,640
Of course, you and that man.

76
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:58,960
Really?

77
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:01,280
Build a love nest together.

78
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:05,800
I'm so happy! If I can live with Ryo-sama,
I'll go to Canada or even the Amazon!

79
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:10,460
But what on earth do you
see in a man like that?

80
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:13,521
That's why, Ai. No matter what you do,

81
00:06:13,571 --> 00:06:15,840
you must not let that man return to Japan.

82
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,340
I understand, Father.

83
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:18,520
What cute ears.

84
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:22,380
No, if only you'd already call me
"Father"...

85
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,240
Ai, Ai.

86
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,760
A deluxe suite room.

87
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:29,660
Everything is going according to plan.

88
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,366
Using the Kanagawa branch
as a stepping stone,

89
00:06:31,416 --> 00:06:35,860
my dream of making Hondara Kenpō the world's
number one martial art is finally about to take off.

90
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:44,320
We've arrived, we've arrived.

91
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,820
No, it looks like we transfer
to another plane from here.

92
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,840
Hey, is there really raw milk around here?

93
00:06:58,840 --> 00:06:59,960
Raw milk?

94
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:02,700
Ryo-sama, what do you mean by raw milk?

95
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:05,870
That's, raw milk, I mean, egg milk,

96
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:09,020
I'm getting all nervous,
I've been asked out on a date,

97
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:11,740
just kidding, just kidding.

98
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:17,000
Hey, where's Canada supposed to be?

99
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:19,000
Didn't we end up in Alaska?

100
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:21,280
This place is fine, you know.

101
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:24,040
Well, it's a thousand tsubo of land,
after all.

102
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:25,960
Well, I suppose it'll be fine.

103
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,160
Phew.

104
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:41,300
Nobody can build houses on ice, can they?

105
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,000
Didn't you get conned?

106
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,080
Who on earth did you buy it from?

107
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:48,120
I-I think it was someone named Hanyu.

108
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:48,640
What?

109
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,080
Aaah!

110
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:54,500
That guy is a notorious
fraudulent real estate agent!

111
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:55,700
Eeeh!

112
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,880
Looks like we got completely screwed.

113
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:58,950
A thousand...

114
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:04,600
He said it was a five-million-yen bargain property,
so I bought it!

115
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:09,440
I-I've been tricked!

116
00:08:09,490 --> 00:08:10,780
Damn you!

117
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:25,480
Oh no, this was an iceberg all along!

118
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:28,860
You bastard! What have you done?!

119
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:32,580
You lying old bastard,
where are the F-cup and G-cup babes?!

120
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,200
No, well, that's...

121
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,020
You son of a bitch!

122
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,260
Hey, stop it!

123
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:37,380
You, you motherfucker!

124
00:08:37,560 --> 00:08:38,200
Stop it, I'm just...

125
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:39,560
What the hell are you talking about,
you idiot! This...

126
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,120
Hey, hey, damn it!

127
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:41,840
Yes!

128
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:44,720
I'll sink you into the icy sea right here!

129
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:45,220
Yes!

130
00:08:45,580 --> 00:08:46,580
Please, stop it!

131
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:49,660
Whoa! My wallet...

132
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,240
My passport is in there too, you know!

133
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:56,100
Without a passport,
I can't get back to Japan!

134
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:56,860
Hmph!

135
00:08:57,020 --> 00:09:00,540
This is payback for costing me 100,000
yen and dragging me to this place!

136
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,720
Father, what are you doing?

137
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:08,140
Hey! That's my passport!

138
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,180
I'm going to use this passport!

139
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:10,960
That's impossible!

140
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:13,180
The photo's different, so it won't work!

141
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:14,860
If I just do this!

142
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:16,540
W-what?!

143
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:16,780
Father!

144
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,180
Look, I've become me!

145
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:20,540
That's totally different!

146
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,520
It's impossible, Father!

147
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:25,260
Let me see your passport.

148
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:28,080
See, your photo doesn't look
anything like you either.

149
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:30,040
The inspector was totally freaking out,
wasn't he?

150
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:32,760
Basically,
it's the real person in Maria's case.

151
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:34,920
Anyway, give back the passport.

152
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,260
You could survive here on your own,
you know.

153
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:38,000
No way.

154
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:39,700
Give me this.

155
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:40,700
I said no.

156
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:41,320
Gimme!

157
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,020
No way.

158
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:42,760
Gimme!

159
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,880
Don't shove your face in mine,
you're so sweltering.

160
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:46,120
Please, just give it to me!

161
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:46,700
No.

162
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:48,340
Don't say that, come on, give it!

163
00:09:48,340 --> 00:09:50,240
No way, please, just gimme!

164
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:50,960
Pleeease!

165
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:51,780
Gimme!

166
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,560
My passport...

167
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:01,620
Good girl, please, bring it over here.

168
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:03,120
Here, over here!

169
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,660
Now we're comrades, aren't we?

170
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:11,980
You dropped that on purpose,
didn't you, you bastard?

171
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:14,060
Why would I do that? It was an accident.

172
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:17,540
I've only got 30 yen in cash.
What are we going to do?

173
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:19,600
I'm completely broke too.

174
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,920
How dare you act so high and mighty,
you bastard!

175
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:30,180
Hey, you too! No, you're the one!
Don't give me that crap, you son of a bitch!

176
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:32,400
Shut up, you idiot!

177
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:39,580
Aaaaah! Get in there! Who do you think you're talking to,
you good-for-nothing?

178
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:46,980
We don't have time to fight! At this rate, we'll end up like that!
No way, I'm not dying in a place like this!

179
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:50,380
I can't even die peacefully! That sound...

180
00:10:50,380 --> 00:10:50,780
That's it...

181
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:52,900
A helicopter!

182
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,420
Heaven hasn't abandoned me!

183
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:57,760
Hey! Help us!

184
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,500
What's wrong, Miss?

185
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:08,060
I thought I heard Ryo-chan's voice just now.

186
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:11,320
He couldn't possibly be out here in the far north of Canada,
could he?

187
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,560
Hey! Help us!

188
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:15,240
It's outside!

189
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:16,180
They don't notice!

190
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:16,880
Notice us!

191
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,140
W-what are you going to do?!

192
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:20,960
We're going to make you hear us.

193
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:22,680
What's your problem?!

194
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,660
George-chan!

195
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:29,780
Reiko!

196
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,320
I've arranged for the passport application.

197
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:40,980
It'll take about two weeks
for the new one to arrive,

198
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:42,620
so make yourselves at home at this hotel.

199
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:44,280
Thank you, Reiko-san.

200
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:47,120
Don't hold back, Maria-chan.

201
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,400
It's our hotel, after all.

202
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:56,620
Meeting you here is a godsend. I'm just
as surprised to see Maria-chan here too.

203
00:11:56,620 --> 00:12:05,460
I got kidnapped! That bookshelf old man said he'd fake my death, and what are you talking about?
You came running just like me, lured in by your biological father!

204
00:12:05,460 --> 00:12:10,540
Biological father? No, I mean, that's
just a joke, just kidding, just kidding.

205
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:20,220
By the way, what are you doing here? Daddy went off to play in the Bahamas,
so I'm taking advantage of the chance to hold meetings and inspections with our affiliated companies.

206
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:22,240
So you weren't just here for fun, then?

207
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:27,040
I finished all my work today, so I plan
to enjoy a vacation starting tomorrow.

208
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,640
That's right. Does anyone want to
go skiing with everyone tomorrow?

209
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:30,900
Sounds good!

210
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,380
I'm not in the mood for that at all.

211
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:34,580
Father.

212
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:38,753
Uncle, I've had someone from our
company look for land for the branch,

213
00:12:38,803 --> 00:12:40,320
so please don't be discouraged.

214
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:44,060
We'll be stuck here for days
until the passport is reissued.

215
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:47,860
Let's just treat this as a vacation and have fun.
Right, Father?

216
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:53,260
Alright, understood.
I'll leave the rest to Reiko.

217
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:55,800
If that's settled, we've got to play,
or it's a total waste!

218
00:12:59,620 --> 00:13:02,060
We only brought leisure gear!

219
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:05,640
There's a real purpose hidden within play.

220
00:13:05,690 --> 00:13:07,600
Alright, let's party hard!

221
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:10,260
Dad bounces back quickly, doesn't he?

222
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:14,100
It's my first time ever having a crush,
so I'm really looking forward to it.

223
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:14,760
Okay!

224
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,480
Enjoy yourselves while you can.

225
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:20,580
I'm going to get my full
revenge on this mutt.

226
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:41,380
Uncle, relax and lower
your hips a little more.

227
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:43,520
Like this, Reiko-dono?

228
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:48,580
Skiing in summer, and on top of that,
being coached by a beautiful instructor!

229
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:49,980
I'm glad we came to Canada.

230
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:50,460
Hey!

231
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:05,980
Big jump!

232
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:08,160
Forward somersault with a twist!

233
00:14:10,940 --> 00:14:12,300
Ryo-sama, you're amazing!

234
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:14,260
How are you so good at this?

235
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:17,370
When it comes to people born
in Tokyo who are good at skiing,

236
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:18,820
it's only the rich ones, but...

237
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,815
When it snows in Tokyo, we common folk

238
00:14:21,865 --> 00:14:24,042
strap on skis we made ourselves from bamboo

239
00:14:24,092 --> 00:14:26,160
and train on the Arakawa embankment.

240
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,980
So my style is self-taught,
like a stray dog's swordsmanship.

241
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,060
But my skills are no worse
than anyone around here.

242
00:14:32,110 --> 00:14:34,160
If it's skiing, I'll teach you.

243
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:37,660
Mind your own business.
I was told by Reiko...

244
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:42,440
I'm personally teaching you,
and this is how you talk to me?

245
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:43,680
Why, you...

246
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:47,520
This is a challenge to me, a martial artist!

247
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:55,640
Hey, wait a second. Let me take off my skis.

248
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:59,020
Alright, let's see you face my true sword!

249
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:11,160
You lovable rascal!

250
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,120
Just say I've mastered it completely.

251
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:15,660
Then I'll teach Maria.

252
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:18,440
We'll learn faster one-on-one.

253
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,840
Even you, Reiko-dono?

254
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,100
Alright, it's settled!

255
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:30,040
First, we'll schuss straight down from the summit,
1,000 meters in one go.

256
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:30,740
No way!

257
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:31,800
What do you mean, "no way"?

258
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:36,380
How dare you speak to your teacher like that!
Cool your head!

259
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:40,180
I never admitted you as a teacher!

260
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:42,080
Just come on already!

261
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:43,240
Where are you going?!

262
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:44,340
Hurry up already!

263
00:15:44,820 --> 00:15:46,220
Is he going to be all right, Dad?

264
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:47,840
Don't worry about it.

265
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,420
Ryo-chan may not look like it, but he's
really good at looking after people.

266
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:52,380
You can't ride the lift?

267
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:54,860
I'm not good with heights.

268
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:59,020
A chance to get revenge for those lost bets.

269
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:01,540
You have to ride the lift
if you want to ski down!

270
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:02,480
Stop it!

271
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:03,140
Get on!

272
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:04,160
Stop it!

273
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:05,580
Let me down!

274
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:06,800
Let go, you idiot!

275
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:12,560
You bastard!

276
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:14,360
Don't shake it!

277
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:16,020
Shut up! I'm sitting there!

278
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,600
Don't climb up on me!
Two people can't sit there!

279
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,760
Then you get off!

280
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:26,640
Damn you!

281
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,180
It's high! Scary! Scary!

282
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:35,380
Me! Hold my hand, hold my hand!

283
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,060
We're going to slide down from here?

284
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:44,380
That's right.

285
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,980
It's almost a right angle!

286
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,720
That's why it's great
practice for right-angle turns.

287
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,900
I don't even know how to turn or stop yet!

288
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,780
I'll teach you while we slide.

289
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:54,200
No way.

290
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,660
This time I'll get my full revenge on you!

291
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:58,920
Hurry up and go!

292
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:06,880
Alright, you're doing great!

293
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:11,700
That's it, like this, like this,
look, look, look, that's it!

294
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:23,360
Got it, there we go.

295
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:28,320
Tag, you old geezer,
you're getting burned by the cold!

296
00:17:29,220 --> 00:17:29,900
What's wrong?

297
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:31,940
I'm covered in snow and my stomach's frozen.

298
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:35,560
What a pathetic dancer you are.
Go take care of it behind that tree.

299
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:36,440
Got it.

300
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:41,400
Doing something like this
in a foreign country...

301
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:45,180
It's getting cold over here, too.

302
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,680
Hey, stop!

303
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:56,860
Idiot, don't come over here!

304
00:17:56,860 --> 00:17:59,780
Stop it!

305
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,600
Fine, but if you climb on me,
I can't stop it!

306
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:05,300
Idiot, take your hands off my pants!

307
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:06,120
You're leaking, aren't you?

308
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:27,000
!

309
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,060
Yay!

310
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:47,640
No matter where we go,
it always ends up like this.

311
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:56,660
The Japanese consulate just contacted us. They said
the passports will be ready the day after tomorrow.

312
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:58,960
That's earlier than expected.

313
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:03,180
What should we do? We can go back to Japan the day after tomorrow.
Should I book the plane tickets?

314
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:07,920
I feel like we should stay a little longer,
but since we basically left without saying anything, we can't.

315
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:09,660
The Chief is furious.

316
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:12,920
There sure are a lot of hunters around here.

317
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:15,780
There's a local hunters'
association meeting going on.

318
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:23,600
I see. By the way, Reiko, you even
took care of the arrangements for us,

319
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:34,100
thank you so much. No, it's nothing much. What was decided is that
we'll be allowed to set up a dojo in this hotel's training room.

320
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:41,140
Good, now you can return to Japan with peace of mind.
Ai and you will have to stay behind. What, you two -

321
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:42,520
I'm going to have you serve as branch chief.

322
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:43,140
Eeeh?

323
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:46,940
There you go, just as you wished,
you two will live here together.

324
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:50,740
But Father, I haven't heard
anything about being branch chief.

325
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:53,660
Since you'll be living together,
isn't that good enough?

326
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,440
Well, yes, but...

327
00:19:55,950 --> 00:19:59,820
Don't joke around! I haven't heard any such thing!
Why am I the branch chief?

328
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:02,980
Yes or no, which is it?

329
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:04,080
No.

330
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:06,020
Which is it?

331
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:07,240
No.

332
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:08,040
Which is it?

333
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:08,780
No.

334
00:20:08,780 --> 00:20:10,360
Which is it?

335
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:16,060
Yes, it's a yes.

336
00:20:16,920 --> 00:20:17,560
Very well.

337
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:21,080
Lady Reiko,
shall we have some tea in the tearoom?

338
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:21,360
Yes.

339
00:20:23,540 --> 00:20:24,980
Lord Ryo, are you all right?

340
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:28,198
You were weak at skiing, though.

341
00:20:28,248 --> 00:20:30,520
Maria, tell me your father's weakness.

342
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:34,562
If this goes on, I'll end up as the branch
chief of that embarrassing police box,

343
00:20:34,612 --> 00:20:36,960
and be stuck living in Canada forever!

344
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:38,920
B-but...

345
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:41,517
Maria, you were tricked too.

346
00:20:41,567 --> 00:20:43,480
Come on, so tell me, Maria.

347
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:47,340
Yes, if Ryo-sama is going to go that far,

348
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:51,520
I think when my father was
training in the mountains,

349
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:54,400
a bear once bit him on the head from behind.

350
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:57,720
After that,
my father seems to really hate bears.

351
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:58,500
That's it!

352
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:00,720
Then if he gets bitten again,

353
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:03,960
he'll never talk about getting
wounds on his body again.

354
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,680
This one's useful.

355
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:12,480
Make sure you sew it on properly.

356
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:14,700
Otherwise it'll look bad.

357
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:15,300
Yes.

358
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:18,180
But since it's the real thing,
it's pretty realistic.

359
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,480
We're hiding here,
so bring the old man over.

360
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:29,360
Yes.

361
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:33,800
I'm going to bite him as hard as I can.

362
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:36,540
Here he comes.

363
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:43,440
- Oh my gosh!
- Watch out!

364
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:44,840
Gyaah!

365
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:52,320
The hunters were gathering! Oh no!

366
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:53,395
Lately,

367
00:21:53,445 --> 00:21:57,540
adults have been scared of me.

368
00:21:57,800 --> 00:21:59,940
I'm dying a little more every day.

369
00:21:59,940 --> 00:22:00,720
Okay!

370
00:22:02,140 --> 00:22:15,066
If we don't find it properly,
we won't be able to get it.

371
00:22:15,116 --> 00:22:18,360
This is...

372
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:20,780
Listen to me!

373
00:22:35,420 --> 00:22:36,740
Is that bear Ryo-chan?

374
00:22:37,740 --> 00:22:39,520
Were you planning to set me up?

375
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:41,660
Got it. I'll arrange it right away.

376
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:53,240
I'm getting my money!

377
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:01,180
Don't shoot! I'm a human!

378
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:11,500
Don't shoot! I'm a Japanese police officer!

379
00:23:13,820 --> 00:23:15,340
We have no choice but to
run into the mountains!

380
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:47,940
It really is me.

381
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:51,420
Damn it! I was screaming while running away,
so my voice is hoarse!

382
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,800
Everyone's a bear with real acting talent

383
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:55,620
I don't know either.

384
00:23:55,940 --> 00:23:59,200
Damn it! Mandala's old man!
You'll pay for this!

385
00:24:04,140 --> 00:24:04,660
Case!

386
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:07,980
Patrol Officer Ryotsu Kankichi,
until ordered by the chief,

387
00:24:08,120 --> 00:24:11,520
is to take on a special assignment at the
restaurant that opened next to the police box,

388
00:24:11,620 --> 00:24:14,720
Why do I have to do a part-time job
that won't even earn me any money?

389
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,760
Writing it together would've been better!

390
00:24:18,220 --> 00:24:21,420
Next time,
"Mimi's Revenge Recipe," see you then!

391
00:24:46,600 --> 00:24:59,420
I want to ride a motorbike across the desert,
I want to be freer than a bird.

392
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:07,140
A lady's dreams changing at
the speed of a kaleidoscope.

393
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:15,240
Love in my heart, sorry, wait for me.

394
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:22,220
The dazzle of living out a panoramic future.

395
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:30,120
You understand, right? Sorry, wait for me.

396
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

